  description:
  - The Emerald Lumen Moths were one of the first newly documented species since
    the Mist entombed the region. The hairs on their upper adbomen secrete an enzyme
    that rapidly encourages growth on select plant protiens, acting as a catalyst
    to a plant's otherwise dormant growth.
  - This coupled with the fact that their hairs carry pollen with ease makes their
    symbiosis with the local flora almost essential for an ecosystem to thrive. A
    decrease in the local moth population could prove devastating to an ecosystem.
  leftText: 
  rightText: The Crimson Lumen Moth is an aggressive subspecies of Lumen Moth that
    sport a long stinger. This stinger was designed to siphon blood out of their
    host, as opposed to injecting venom. Unlike their passive counterparts, these
    travel in dense swarms and reside within hives, characteristics more similar
    to that of bees and wasps. A lone specimen is indicitive of an exiled monarch.
